    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "HERE COMES THE MUSEUM. Beatlemania is on the rise again: four biopics on the British band are slated for release next year and now, Liverpool, the Beatles’ home city, has announced that it’s moving the Beatles Story Museum to a new 100,000-square-foot location in the city, according to The Times of London . Ownership of the museum is also being handed over to the Beatles’ media company Apple Corps, who has also acquired the St Johns Beacon, Liverpool’s second-tallest building, which will be used as a separate attraction themed around the 1968 animated musical Yellow Submarine . The project is scheduled to finish by 2028. Paul McCartney has called the project “extraordinary” and British Prime Minister Andy Burnham has said this is the “kind of ambition I want to see more of across Britain.”",
