    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The Kicker"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "FOUR STRIKES . The Victoria & Albert Museum ’s unionized staff is planning to strike across all four of the museum’s London sites on October 29 and 30, reported Hyperallergic . Since the summer, V&A staff have been demanding better pay and working conditions, citing lack of hydration breaks and restroom use at the newly opened V&A East Storehouse. Prospect Union’s general secretary, Mike Clancy, said in a statement that “Prospect members are dedicated to their jobs, and it is these dedicated staff who make the museum the world-class attraction it is” and that the museum’s director, Tristram Hunt, has been refusing to participate in negotiations.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Hyperallergic",
          "url": "https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fe.mail.artnews.com%2Fclick%3FZTNDBS8MwFMfx_C0577E0bdJkJ2UKIrKL4sHLeE1et2LTjCS1iPi_S0Fl5w_vfeF3fw7xjCGQv8FUJlry2mP7Lx4Gz3e8aq1UppVW1Y2RTimhVNMZ6_mGu8J3_BIcYCqwngIJLbyywhvqVGfaSvra9sqZtpUNaYSKb3ha_17F-Dd7_R_h80IJx5HSaXArbj8AIcyZ5gC5YN9DpgIlQi5peCdAl2LOgOMIfZwTjHHycYI8FMpb9vz2cAw4OUwTLce7w8vtoRKykkJqJ2ttm0azJ0yanbAM0i_s8Y_3v_wzAAer348fc4a5&data=05%7C02%7Chmohammed%40artnews.com%7C44d763821f784bc37fd508df2f72b64b%7Ce950f25546e44144a778a6ff4f557492%7C0%7C0%7C639281841880468586%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=ISJrD76fQbLaO1YysYnrj5kARpP2n0uHM5eFS46%2Fuac%3D&reserved=0"
